# Doc Gate (soft)

Before PDP or design-doc work, run a quick gate. Do **not** invent a winner when sources disagree — ask.

Full workflow: `.cursor/skills/doc-gate/SKILL.md` (load when conflicts, multi-doc tasks, or unclear round).

## 1) Active target

Read `docs/rounds/README.md` for which route is **Active** vs **Frozen**.

- Default new work → the **Active** route (today `/v6` / r7 unless the index says otherwise).
- Touching a Frozen route requires an explicit user ask.

## 2) Authority order (highest wins)

From `docs/pdp-paper-source-of-truth.md`:

1. Approved Paper (exact page / frame / node)
2. Explicit designer direction in this thread
3. Existing production code
4. Internal docs and workshop notes

If code and Paper disagree → Paper wins. If docs and Paper disagree → Paper wins.

## 3) Stale / superseded docs

Ignore or demote docs that say **Superseded**, **one-time audit**, or map an older round than the Active target — unless the task is explicitly about that frozen round.

Canonical entry points:

| Need | Open first |
|------|------------|
| Versions / flags | `docs/pdp-versions.md` |
| Round status / links | `docs/rounds/README.md` |
| Paper parity policy | `docs/pdp-paper-source-of-truth.md` |
| Deploy / share | `docs/deploy-and-links.md` |
| Active round changelog | matching file under `docs/rounds/` |

## 4) When to stop and ask (≤ 2 questions)

Ask before coding when any of these are true:

- Request targets a Frozen version without saying so
- Two docs (or doc vs Paper) disagree on the same module
- User cites a superseded page as if it were current
- Change would rewrite v1 data, unscoped `globals.css`, or skip `PdpVersionConfig` flags

Format: state the conflict in one line → give 2–3 options with one-line tradeoffs → one direct question.

## 5) When not to block

Proceed without questions when the Active target is clear, the cited doc matches that round, and nothing conflicts with Paper / version rules.
